HOW TO RUN RECALL
=================

Easiest way (Windows)
---------------------
1. Install Node.js LTS from https://nodejs.org.
2. Double-click "Start Recall.cmd" in this folder.
3. Keep the window open and use http://localhost:5173.

Any operating system
--------------------
1. Install Node.js 20.19+ or 22.12+.
2. Open a terminal in this folder.
3. Run: npm install
4. Run: npm start
5. Open http://localhost:5173.

To stop
-------
Press Ctrl+C in the terminal, or close the command window.

Notes
-----
- The first launch needs internet access to install dependencies.
- Review data is stored in your browser at http://localhost:5173.
- Export a backup from Settings before clearing browser data.
